From 316f1b182dc6808d3c3f571d3c3d8174320275bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaul Lavochkin <shaul9191@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:15:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] wasm: optional await hooks in the printer for a host
 engine without AsyncContext

BUNWASM_AWAIT_HOOKS (off by default) prints async-context hooks so a host
JS engine without AsyncContext can carry AsyncLocalStorage across
suspensions, rejected awaits included. bun-wasm's browser engine turns it
on around its runtime transpiles.

An async body without its own `try` or `for await` prints `await x` as
`__bunwasm_resume(__bunwasm_capture(), await x)`. Any other async body (an
"S body", including a module top level that awaits) declares
`let __bunwasm_s = 0;` after its directives and prints:

- `await x` as `__bunwasm_resumed(await __bunwasm_id(x, __bunwasm_s =
  __bunwasm_capture()), __bunwasm_s, __bunwasm_s = 0)`, so a rejection
  leaves the frame of the suspension in `__bunwasm_s`;
- `__bunwasm_caught(__bunwasm_s, __bunwasm_s = 0);` first in every
  `catch` and `finally` block, which re-enters that frame;
- async generator `yield x` as `__bunwasm_id(yield __bunwasm_id(x,
  __bunwasm_s = __bunwasm_capture()), __bunwasm_s = 0)`;
- `for await` in a block holding `let __bunwasm_c`, with the iterable in
  `__bunwasm_id` and the body in a try/finally that records the frame of
  the next implicit await on every exit. Only the outermost label opens
  the block, so labeled `continue` still targets the loop.

BUNWASM_HOOKS_VERSION (2) versions these shapes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
